  "worked_solution": "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061z & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}\u2061z & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-c \\\\ z & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-c}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get a family of curves:\n\n$$\nz={e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-c},\\,c\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$",
